<title>JAPAN: Japan May imported vehicle sales down 27.0 pct y/y.</title>
<headline>Japan May imported vehicle sales down 27.0 pct y/y.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Domestic sales of imported vehicles in Japan fell 27.0 percent in May from a year earlier to 22,919 units, the Japan Automobile Importers' Association (JAIA) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>It was the second successive month that sales dropped on a year-on-year basis.  </p>
<p>The May breakdown of imported vehicles, with percentage</p>
<p>changes from a year earlier, was as follows:</p>
<p> Cars (total)	   21,268  down 25.5 percent</p>
<p>- Cars 2001cc or more 13,951  down 32.9 percent - Cars 2000cc or less  7,317  down  6.0 percent  Trucks (total)	  1,650  down 41.2 percent</p>
<p> - Heavy		   1,417  down 29.2 percent</p>
<p> - Light		     233  down 71.0 percent</p>
<p> Buses			   1  down 85.7 percent</p>
<p>Exporting countries' and selected manufcaturers' car sales</p>
<p>in Japan in May, with percentage changes from a year earlier:</p>
<p> German (total)		 11,482  down 17.2 percent</p>
<p>  Volkswagen Audi Group	4,142  up    2.5 percent</p>
<p>  -Volkswagen		    3,451  up    7.7 percent</p>
<p>  -Audi				691  down 17.5 percent</p>
<p>  Adam Opel			2,082  down 35.0 percent</p>
<p>  BMW				2,034  down 21.6 percent</p>
<p>  Mercedes-Benz		  2,757  down 21.2 percent</p>
<p>  Ford-Werke AG		    220  down 32.9 percent</p>
<p>  Porsche			    234  up   18.2 percent</p>
<p> United States (total)	 4,908  down 38.1 percent</p>
<p>  Honda USA			1,672  down 42.0 percent</p>
<p>  Ford Motor			 445  down 55.5 percent</p>
<p>  General Motors		 1,296  down  0.8 percent</p>
<p>  Toyota			     208  down 86.9 percent</p>
<p>  Chrysler			   901  down 16.2 percent</p>
<p> Sweden (total)		  1,478  down 39.9 percent</p>
<p>  Volvo			    1,463  down 38.8 percent</p>
<p>  Saab				  15  down 78.3 percent</p>
<p> Britain (total)		 1,821  down 11.9 percent</p>
<p>  Rover group		    1,490  down 17.1 percent</p>
<p>  Jaguar			     168  down 18.4 percent</p>
<p>  Nissan			     121  vs		nil</p>
<p> France (total)		    584  down 31.5 percent</p>
<p>  Peugeot Citroen		  453  down 26.7 percent</p>
<p>  - Peugeot			  277  down 19.9 percent</p>
<p>  - Citroen			  176  down 35.3 percent</p>
<p>  Renault			    131  down 44.3 percent</p>
<p> Italy (total)		     617  up    8.8 percent</p>
<p>  Fiat group			 602  up   10.7 percent</p>
<p> Spain (total)		     187  down 70.0 percent</p>
<p>  Nissan			     187  down 70.0 percent</p>
<p> Netherlands			 118  vs		nil</p>
<p>  Mitsubishi			 118  vs		nil</p>
<p> Australia			    13  down 89.2 percent</p>
<p>  Mitsubishi			  13  down 89.2 percent</p>
<p>General Motors' May car sales included 598 Cavaliers sold by Toyota, up 26.7 percent year-on-year. The May total included 173 Nissan AD vans made in Mexico, down 77.0 percent from the year before.</p>
<p>Of the total, sales of vehicles produced by overseas units of Japanese carmakers totalled 2,517 in May, down 58.3 percent from a year earlier.</p>
